# WS2-05. The condition is bound in a let so the temporary's drop point is the let
# statement's end under every reading of spec/04 §3. # Sources: spec/04-expressions.md §3 (temporaries, including inside nested calls and aggregate literals, live until the end of the statement and drop there in reverse creation order; only the chosen ?: arm and the needed && / || operand evaluate) and spec/03 §5.
The right operand (and its temporary) exists only when c is true.
profiles: host
with: tok.clo
expect: output
contrast: == 3) ==> == 4)
contrast-expect: output
--- output
no
drop 3
yes
end
--- contrast-output
no
drop 3
no
end
